cant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOKUBO TADASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO TAKEAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOKUBO, TADASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO, TAKEAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A novel polymeric material for artificial bones, characterized by comprising a solid or gel-form base which comprises as the main component either a polysaccharide having carboxyl groups or groups derived therefrom or a polysaccharide having incorporated therein carboxyl groups or groups derived therefrom and which has calcium ions bonded thereto. It has the excellent ability to form apatite.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un matériau polymère pour os artificiel, qui comprend une base solide ou sous forme de gel dont l'élément essentiel est un polysaccharide à groupes carboxyliques ou groupes dérivés de ce type de groupe, ou bien un polysaccharide renfermant des groupes carboxyle ou des groupes dérivés de ce type de groupe, avec des ions de calcium liés à la structure considérée. Le matériau en question a une excellente aptitude à la formation d'apatite.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://ww